From: Soe Thura <6492082+thixpin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 14:36:46 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Translate blrl as an indirect call

Forza Motorsport 4 calls a function pointer once with mtlr and blrl, which the recompiler
rejects. blrl branches to LR and sets LR to the following address: the target is read before LR
is written, then called indirectly as bctrl does. With skip_lr, LR is not available and blrl
stays fatal.
---
 XenonRecomp/recompiler.cpp | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/XenonRecomp/recompiler.cpp b/XenonRecomp/recompiler.cpp
index cf01d30..1688fb1 100644
--- a/XenonRecomp/recompiler.cpp
+++ b/XenonRecomp/recompiler.cpp
@@ -854,7 +854,16 @@ bool Recompiler::Recompile(
         break;
 
     case PPC_INST_BLRL:
-        Fatal(fmt::format("blrl at {:X} is not supported", base));
+        // Indirect call through LR: the target is LR before it is set to the return address.
+        if (config.skipLr)
+        {
+            Fatal(fmt::format("blrl at {:X} needs LR, which skip_lr removes", base));
+            break;
+        }
+        println("\t{}.u64 = ctx.lr;", temp());
+        println("\tctx.lr = 0x{:X};", base + 4);
+        println("\tPPC_CALL_INDIRECT_FUNC({}.u32);", temp());
+        csrState = CSRState::Unknown; // the call could change it
         break;
 
     case PPC_INST_BLT:
